Collected: 2026-09-29
Licence: public-domain
Sources:
- NOAA National Geodetic Survey, GRAV-D (Gravity for the Redefinition of the American Vertical
  Datum), Block EN02 release BETA2 <https://geodesy.noaa.gov/GRAV-D/>
Evidence class (rule 10): check
Where the Earth's radius enters:
- g: NOAA removed the Eötvös effect with the GRS80 radii; putting it back needs those radii
- ve, vn: velocities from the published positions on the GRS80 ellipsoid (computed by fog)
What would vindicate the flat model (rule 5): Uncorrected airborne gravity that agrees between
  eastbound and westbound lines, or a best fraction of the globe's Eötvös correction of 0 rather
  than 1.
